course: dictionary
lesson: 5099
title: Words in the middle
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Intermediate means in the middle, between two levels, stages or places. A beginner is at the start, an advanced learner is near the top, and an intermediate learner is somewhere between them.
explain: «For several weeks he refuses his meals or intermediate light refreshments.» The clue is the words around it: meals are the big parts of the day, so intermediate light refreshments must be snacks that come in between them.
explain: Use the swap check. Put «snacks between meals» into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does, so your meaning is right.
fact: Intermediate means in the middle, between two levels, stages or places.
fact: «Intermediate» can describe a person who is not a beginner but not yet an expert, as in «an intermediate swimmer».
fact: In maths, «intermediate steps» are the working between the question and the answer.
fact: In science, a chrysalis is the intermediate stage between caterpillar and butterfly.
fact: As a noun, an intermediate is a person at a middle level.
exercise: Ms Lee's club has beginner, intermediate and advanced groups. Which group is in the middle? | Advanced | *Intermediate | Beginner
exercise: «He ate his meals and intermediate light refreshments.» What are intermediate light refreshments? | Medicine for sick people | Big dinners at night | *Snacks between meals
exercise: In maths, what are «intermediate steps»? | *The working between the question and the answer | The question copied out again | The final answer written in a box
test: Ravi swims well, but he is not yet an expert. Which word describes him? | Advanced | Beginner | Champion | *Intermediate
test: A chrysalis is the ___ stage between caterpillar and butterfly. Which word fills the gap? | First | *Intermediate | Sleepy | Last
exam: «Intermediate» means between two things. Which sentence uses it correctly? | Lily ate an intermediate breakfast at the very start of the day | *Lily was an intermediate swimmer, not a beginner but not yet an expert | Lily was intermediate, so she never swims at all
